# Corpus recordings: exact PTY byte streams captured with ptyrec (PTYREC1
# format, see src/corpus.rs). All at 50x120, TERM=xterm-256color, driven by
# piped keystroke scripts with sleeps between phases.
#
# NEVER re-capture to fix a failing test — goldens re-baseline only with a
# REBASELINE: note (docs/roadmap.md, Guardrails).
#
# file                app + version              what it exercises
vim.ptyrec            NVIM v0.12.4 (-u NONE)     alt screen, scroll regions, split windows, Ctrl-D/U paging
less.ptyrec           less 704                   paging, search highlight, alt-screen quit/restore
fzf.ptyrec            fzf 0.74.1                 fullscreen redraws, live filtering, cursor movement
htop.ptyrec           htop 3.5.2 (nixpkgs)       heavy SGR color, meters, full-screen refresh
timg-kitty.ptyrec     timg 1.6.3 (-pk, f=100)    kitty graphics APC transmit+display, terminal probes (CSI 16t, DA1, DSR, >q)
claude.ptyrec         claude 2.1.226             trust dialog, Write-tool permission prompt, spinner phase, tool result, Ctrl-C exit
pi.ptyrec             pi 0.84.1 (qwen3.6 local)  streamed reply, braille Working... status footer, model line, Ctrl-D exit
#
# claude/pi captured via a scripted expect-style PTY driver feeding ptyrec's
# stdin (session bytes are a real session; only the typist was scripted).
# Terminal-identity env (KITTY_*, TERM_PROGRAM, ...) stripped so agents see
# plain xterm-256color — pi otherwise floods kitty-graphics retransmits.
